  "summary": "A pipe tracing system adds heat to a pipe to replace what it loses through its insulation, keeping the product above its freezing, congealing or crystallisation temperature (for example caustic and liquor lines in alumina refineries, heavy fuel oil, sulphur and water lines in winter). Steam tracing uses small tubes carrying steam alongside the pipe, drained by a trap; electric tracing uses a self-regulating heating cable controlled by a thermostat.",
